; link/pop_msys.link — the MUSIC PLAYER as a DISK-RESIDENT unit (P4.19).
;
; ★★★ IT IS NOT IN THE LOADM IMAGE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. P3.4 established the
; intro's shape: the LOADM'd program stays ONE GRANULE and everything else is read by the
; HAL's WD1773 primitive once DECB has finished — the caption bundle, every screen, the
; scene program, the scene bundle and four cel pages all arrive that way. intro_seq.s:51
; puts it plainly: "that is exactly why the assets are READ here rather than LOADED here."
;
; ★★ P4.19 IGNORED THAT AND PAID FOR IT. Linking the player into INTROSEQ.BIN took the
; image from 2,215 B of payload to 5,317 and LOADM truncated — the suite read $7900..$7D43
; as "34..00" against "34..39", the kernel segment begun and not finished. The ceiling was
; only ever in play because the player was in the wrong kind of file.
;
; ★ AND READING IT INSTEAD MOVES THE FLOOR. $0E00 was the lowest address a LOADM SEGMENT
; could survive (DECB's file buffers reach above $0A00 — measured: $0D00 loads and runs
; with silently damaged data). A disk READ happens long after DECB is done, so the whole
; of $0A00..$1FFF is available: 5,632 B against the player's 3,102.
;
;   $0A00-$1B67   THE PLAYER, 4,456 B, READ from disk track 32
;   $1B68-$1FFF   free, 1,176 B of margin below the engine
;   $2000-$24FF   engine (LOADM'd)
;   $2600-$2AA6   scene program (read from disk, same mechanism)
;   $3000-$52FF   caption bundle (read from disk, same mechanism)
;
; The entry symbol is nominal: this unit is a library the engine calls, not a program the
; operator EXECs. lwlink --decb requires one, and decb_to_raw discards it.

section msys load 0A00

entry msys_entry
